// Teuhill

#define DETAIL_TEXT_SANITARIUM "\"The rumour circles that the reason for the uncommon scale, grandeur and complexity of the facilities of the Sanitarium is the interesting popularity of the Town with Psydonian pilgirms. \n\ Those devoted men and women of the Old Faith flocked to the Town, as a resting stop before pilgrimaging out to the Weeping Grove, and then further south towards the Unforgotten Fortress. \n\ But the roads and paths of the Grove oft times proved dangerous and treacherous, and with their own faith standing inbetween their broken bodies and the grace of the Ten Saints, they found themselves in need for a more impartial place of healing. \n\
With time, the clergy of the Otavan Orthodoxy finally managed to gather the funds to construct a marvelous, stone hall, meant for a group of more.. religiously tolerant healers. \n\ Conflict with local religious authorities soon arose. The local clergymen disliked the power slipping from their grasp, and soon they strongarmed the Ducal Family into permitting the Sanitarium be built outside the Walls of the Town."
#define DETAIL_TEXT_PILFIELD "\"Although at first sight it might seem that the Village of Pilgrim's Field is infact, simply a continous part of the City of Teuhill, only, outside of the protection of it's stony walls, the small Village is in it's own, covolutedly-legalese way, a completely separate entity. \n\ The Town, in the past and in the present and, hopefully also in the future, tends to enjoy a steady and sizeable amount of Psydonite Pilgirms, looking out to pay their respects at the now-swamped entrance to the Unforgotten Fortress. \n\ In time, the local Clergy devoted to the Worship of the Ten grew tired and ired at the continous and unashamed romancing of the political and economical elite, and the unending masses of, what in their mind were, blasphemous fools. \n\
Threathening to petition the Holy See for a more direct intervention, the local Tennite clergy managed to finally push the ruling family into outlawing the presence of Psydonites within the city limits. \n\ The Pilgrims, unabashed and greatly unwilling to stop their travels to their rememberance sites, simply began setting up tents and shanty towns directly outside the city walls. \n\ With time, the opportunities that the presence of the Psydonites provided, greatly outshined any potential ire that the clergy could dish out at the Town's merchant class, and booths and smaller shops began setting up outside of the city walls, servicing the many faithful found therein. \n\
With the coming of reign of Queen Alexia, blessed be her name, The Tyrant forever guiding her reign, the agreements with the Holy Mission of the Otavan Orthodoxy, to most known simply as the Otavan Inquisition, also mandated the reversal of the ban on the presence of Psydonites within the city. Although by that point, Pilgirm's Field, as it came to be known, was already a prospering village."
#define DETAIL_TEXT_FORGOTTENTEMPLE "He... can't really be dead, can He..?"
#define DETAIL_TEXT_TEUHILL "\"Teuhill is a County, with its capital located in the Town bearing the same name. \n\ The County of Teuhill is, de jure, part of the Duchy of Rockhill, albeit, due to being a potential breeding ground for religious conflict, Kingsfield's eye is focused upon it much more often when comapred to its peers. \n\ The Elves claim that the Town- or at least the region immediately surrounding it, was once home to an ancient druidic cult, focused around worshipping, and preserving the Grove. \n\ Psydonite pilgrims headed to the Weeping Grove, and Noccite scholars heading towards the Bluewater Forests are the lyfeline of the Town, and quite probably the reason why it's not yet abandonded. \n\ Religious conflict is common occurence within the County, The Comital family oft being forced to act as mediators between the Psydonites and Tennites."
#define DETAIL_TEXT_TEUHILL_KEEP "\"The Castle of Teuhill was originally erected hundred of yils ago, as a personal retreat for the Ferentian Royalty, since then, countless disputes, treaties, backstabbings and all the other possible political games that have been played, left it as a County under the Duchy of Rockhill. This is why the Teuhill Keep is much larger and more grandeur in its design when compared to other Comital holdings. \n\ The size of the Teuhill Keep is often times used by the local nobility as a reason to boast and bragg about their supposed power and wealth. It is also, possibly even more often, used as a reason to insult them, citing their supposed need to 'compensate' for 'something'. "
